# Aninda Studio — what is deliberately not committed.
#
# Note what is NOT here: the generated trees. `07_tokens/build`, `07_tokens/css`,
# `04_mark/svg`, `08_components/cards`, `12_packages` and the guidebook are all
# committed on purpose. That is what lets CI regenerate them and fail on any
# difference — a gitignored output cannot be proved unedited.

# ── The project-local sandbox. Rebuilt by 00_sandbox, never shipped. ──────────
.venv/
node_modules/
00_sandbox/browsers/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ── Working files from a build or a check run ─────────────────────────────────
_shot.png
_review_pages/
_review_pages2/
*.tmp
.playwright/

# ── macOS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store

# ── Isolated worktrees used by the review rounds ──────────────────────────────
# Each reviewer gets its own checkout here so it can run write-capable generators
# and break them freely without touching the real tree. Round 1 of this review
# originally ran without isolation: a reviewer edited the colour engine to test
# whether its guard fires, reverted the source but left the output, and the light
# theme's ink was silently left near-white. These are disposable by design.
.claude/worktrees/

# ── The superseded Aninda drafts ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The pre-decision reference sheet and benchmark were copied in at the start as
# input. They were never removed, so the published repository shipped a page that
# draws the mark as the lowercase 'd' the project abandoned, alongside a palette,
# type stack and tile radius that are all superseded. Chapter 03 names that 'd' as
# "the one mistake this mark has already made" — so the repo documented the error
# and distributed it at the same time. They are gone; this stops them returning.
_reference/
